scripts/sprint-runner.ts reads a sprint JSON and spawns orchestrate-agents-v2.ts. The orchestrator expects tasks with fields: id, title, agent, type, priority, dependencies[], status, context (string prompt), deliverables.code[], task_target.

But CEO-authored sprints use a different schema: description (instead of context), depends_on[] (instead of dependencies[]), acceptance (extra field), file (single string instead of deliverables.code[]). This mismatch means CEO-authored sprints produce empty context for every task.

Fix: After reading the sprint JSON and before writing logs/sprint-runner-active.json, add a normalizeTasks() function that maps CEO schema → orchestrator schema. Add ONLY this function and one call site — do not change any other logic.

Add this function to sprint-runner.ts:

function normalizeTasks(tasks: any[]): any[] {
  return tasks.map((task: any) => ({
    ...task,
    // CEO schema → orchestrator schema (only fill if orchestrator field is absent)
    context: task.context ?? task.description ?? '',
    dependencies: task.dependencies ?? task.depends_on ?? [],
    deliverables: task.deliverables ?? (task.file ? { code: [task.file] } : { code: [] }),
    // Defaults for required orchestrator fields that CEO schema omits
    agent: task.agent ?? 'coder',
    type: task.type ?? 'feature',
    priority: task.priority ?? 'medium',
    status: task.status ?? 'pending',
  }));
}

Call it: sprint.tasks = normalizeTasks(sprint.tasks);
Place the call AFTER sprint.tasks is loaded and BEFORE writing to logs/sprint-runner-active.json.

